    "steps": [
        {
            "step_number": 1,
            "title": "Power Cord",
            "content": [
                "Remove the two silicone covers which encase the screws.",
                "Remove both 1 mm screws using a T5 Torx screwdriver.",
                "Pry open the plastic cover starting from the top of the iron."
            ],
            "images": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/fTS42B6ZSHPgur2t.medium",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/NUGgrgiGk3urs2EY.medium",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/BgmHWQeIUN6CLtmb.medium"
            ],
            "images_200x150": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/fTS42B6ZSHPgur2t.200x150",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/NUGgrgiGk3urs2EY.200x150",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/BgmHWQeIUN6CLtmb.200x150"
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/155951/325789",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        },
        {
            "step_number": 2,
            "content": [
                "Remove both caps from the end of the wire by using pliers.",
                "Unfold the metal in the caps using the pliers to release the exposed wire.",
                "Remove the two 1 mm screws holding down the wire using a Phillips #00 screwdriver.",
                "Once the wires are exposed separate and fold to opposite sides."
            ],
            "images": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/21YKolOJBQDGJSJ1.medium"
            ],
            "images_200x150": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/21YKolOJBQDGJSJ1.200x150",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/FUcQkqJVZBCEYZoU.200x150",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/XOqPDLIwTUcLYrnL.200x150"
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/155951/325790",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        },
        {
            "step_number": 3,
            "content": [
                "Remove the old power cord from the iron completely.",
                "Insert the new cord through the plastic cover and hole of the iron as demonstrated in the image."
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/155951/325791",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        },
        {
            "step_number": 4,
            "content": [
                "Expose about half an inch of wire by removing the silicone that encases it.",
                "Tie the new wire into a knot and connect the wires accordingly.",
                "Place the caps over the exposed wire and use pliers to tighten the metal to secure the wire."
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/155951/325792",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        },
        {
            "step_number": 5,
            "content": [
                "Once the caps are over the wires add the two 1 mm Phillips screws along with the small base plate which secures the wire.",
                "When all wires are secure place the plastic cover and screw back in the 1mm Torx screws."
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/155951/325794",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        }
    ],
    "conclusion": "Finish Line",
